# BVLL-IPv6 (Annex U.2), each function as Wireshark's packet-bvlc.c lays it
# out: type 82, function, length, the sender's virtual MAC, then the
# function's fields. 000257 is device 599's VMAC; 00000a device 10's.

82 02 00 0f 00 02 57 01 20 ff ff 00 ff 10 08 => original-broadcast from 000257 npdu 0120ffff00ff1008
82 01 00 0e 00 02 57 00 00 0a 01 00 10 08 => original-unicast from 000257 to 00000a npdu 01001008
82 03 00 0a 00 02 57 00 00 0a => address-resolution from 000257 for 00000a
82 05 00 0a 00 00 0a 00 02 57 => address-resolution-ack from 00000a to 000257
82 06 00 07 00 02 57 => virtual-address-resolution from 000257
82 07 00 0a 00 00 0a 00 02 57 => virtual-address-resolution-ack from 00000a to 000257
# A BBMD relaying a foreign device's resolution, with the asker's address.
82 04 00 1c 00 02 57 00 00 0a fe 80 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01 ba c0 => forwarded-address-resolution from 000257 for 00000a origin [fe80::1]:47808
82 08 00 1d 00 02 57 20 01 0d b8 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 05 ba c0 01 00 10 08 => forwarded from 000257 origin [2001:db8::5]:47808 npdu 01001008
82 09 00 09 00 02 57 00 3c => register-foreign-device from 000257 ttl 60
82 0a 00 19 00 02 57 20 01 0d b8 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 05 ba c0 => delete-fdt-entry from 000257 [2001:db8::5]:47808
82 00 00 09 00 02 57 00 00 => result from 000257 0x0000
82 00 00 09 00 02 57 00 90 => result from 000257 0x0090
82 0c 00 0f 00 02 57 01 20 ff ff 00 ff 10 08 => distribute-broadcast from 000257 npdu 0120ffff00ff1008
# Secure-BVLL alone carries no virtual MAC.
82 0b 00 06 aa bb => secure-bvll data aabb
82 0d 00 08 00 02 57 01 => unknown 13 from 000257 data 01
